+// ---- grouped by expert (README step 55): an expert used by several tokens of a chunk is read
+// once for all of them. canon_group_kernel sorts the chunk's (slot, pair) keys (pair = t k + j)
+// in one block and marks the runs of equal slots; the grouped kernels then run one block row per
+// group, loading each weight block once and applying it to the group's tokens kCanonTB at a time.
+// Per (row, token) the operations and their order are canon_rows', so the rows are the same bits.
+
+constexpr int kGroupMax = 4096;  // pairs per chunk (M k)
+constexpr int kCanonTB = 4;      // tokens per pass over an expert's weights
